<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79958" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παστάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>porch in front of the house</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.148
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				169
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>colonnade</i>, such as ran round temples, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.8.9
			</span></i>(pl.), prob. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραστάσι</span>
			in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hier.</u>
				11.2
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς δὲ παστάδας κοινὰς εἶμεν
				πάντεσσι</span>, at Delphi, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1126.22
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				42(1).109
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				 ii 122
			</span></i> (Epid.) ; = Lat. <i>porticus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				4.44
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Galb.</u>
				25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>part of the house next the porch, hall</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.789
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.172
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>inner room, bridal chamber</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκτέριστον ἀμφὶ π</span>., of the cave in which Antigone
			was immured, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1207
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεδρωτὰ παστάδων τέραμνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1371
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				24.46
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.245
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphan.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Menemach.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				10.14.3
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παστάδος ὥρη</span>, of
			marriageable age, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				521
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thessalonica</span>), cf.Chor.in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rev.Phil.</u>
				1.241
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμοιρος ἔτι παστάδος</span>,
			of a bachelor, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Proc.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>.</div>
